# Checked pair products for a native all-row-two eight

The source kernel words with masks 1, 6, and 6607 generate the eight used
in `NonLineEight`. Seven distinct displacement products cover its 21
unordered independent pairs. Two explicit row-span inclusions and pivot
columns certify rank sixteen for each product. All matrix multiplications
are checked by Lean's kernel; no external computation is trusted.

The coordinates reuse the original ATLAS max2 factor ordering from
`TwoCoreCentralizer.Generation.LowerBound.KernelSeparation`, whose source
directory retains attribution. The rank-certificate interface is the
existing local involution census. This checks the unrestricted container
step suggested by Kleidman--Wilson (1988), Section 2.1, pp.488--489;
it does not assert maximal-two-locality of the resulting example.
-/

